{
  "info": {
    "name": "Black Box: PayPal sandbox calls",
    "description": "Every PayPal REST call Black Box makes, in the order a case uses them: the shop takes payment with the agent's record hash in `custom_id`, a buyer disputes, and Black Box reads the dispute and carries out its verdict. Each request names the file that makes it; method, path and body match the code.\n\nSandbox only. Set `client_id` and `client_secret` (the merchant's sandbox REST app) and run **Get access token** first. The payout requests use the agent operator's own app: `operator_client_id`, `operator_client_secret`, then **Get operator access token**.\n\nRequests that move sandbox money: Capture order, Create order with saved wallet, Accept claim, Make offer, Create payout.\n\nBuilt by `node postman/build.mjs`; see `postman/README.md`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
